      ":question/problem": "![](images/1c/1cc703af7ccf4aaf89f80449ec0eef96c0d1d1e2268b781f6ffc45fd495eb1c3.png)\n\nRobert was $20m$ from the base of a wooden electric pole when he noticed that the angle from the ground to the top of the pole was $45^{\u2218}$. If the pole is tilted $80^{\u2218}$ from the ground towards Robert, as shown above, then what is the height of the pole to one decimal place?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
